# woods: the old woods beside the reference game's settlement (the owner, 25 November: doc/design/direction-2026-11-25-reference-game.md §3; register OR-611), entered at once from the heart of the town.
// A Kyr template (see src/world/kyr-template.ts), written for the reference settlement only (ReferenceSettlement).
// {t} is the town's id, {town} its name, {w} the deep place under the woods and {site} its name, {old} the first
// makers as the folk call them, {dealer} the one in the town who buys what the woods give and hears what is seen in
// them; {!wet} and {!windy} are the country's wet and windy weathers as its sky has them. Several places of their own in the woods, none on the way to another: two known from the first (the old
// ride and the burners' clearing), one found by its tracks (the wallow), and the fallen stones, seen from the ride up
// under the beeches (the slope up from the ride, or the deer-path from the burners' clearing); and between the stones the way down, in plain sight once the company stands there (the owner's
// playtest of 27 November, OR-1501: the dungeon had been hard to find, circled for; its mouth is a named, seen place,
// never found by circling). What is under it, and what the old ones cut there, is still found out by asking. Every way in the woods takes time,
// and the woods are dark at night; there is a beast in them that will fight for its ground. Nothing here is an errand.
--- base
  Place {t}_wood "the old woods above {town}" is site within {t} at 0, 4.
  Place {t}_wood_edge "the edge of the old woods" is room within {t}_wood at 1, 2 outdoors.
  Place {t}_wood_ride "the old ride" is room within {t}_wood at 1, 1 outdoors.
  Place {t}_wood_burners "the charcoal-burners' clearing" is room within {t}_wood at 2, 1 outdoors.
  Place {t}_wood_wallow "the boar's wallow" is room within {t}_wood at 0, 1 outdoors.
  Place {t}_wood_stones "the fallen stones under the beeches" is room within {t}_wood at 1, 0 outdoors.
  Passage {t}_wood_path "the path up into the old woods" is path between {t}_green and {t}_wood_edge taking 15 minutes.
  Passage {t}_wood_into "the old ride under the trees" is path between {t}_wood_edge and {t}_wood_ride taking 30 minutes.
  Passage {t}_wood_burnway "the burners' track" is path between {t}_wood_ride and {t}_wood_burners taking 20 minutes.
  Passage {t}_wood_runs "the boar-runs through the holly" is path between {t}_wood_ride and {t}_wood_wallow taking 30 minutes hidden until {t}_wood_tracks.
  Passage {t}_wood_beeches "the deer-path up under the beeches" is path between {t}_wood_burners and {t}_wood_stones taking 30 minutes.
  Passage {t}_wood_slope "the slope up to the stones" is path between {t}_wood_ride and {t}_wood_stones taking 30 minutes.
  Passage {t}_wood_down "the dark slot between the fallen stones" is stair between {t}_wood_stones and {w} hidden until {t}_wood_door.
  Observe {t}_wood_edge_scene at {t}_wood_edge as fixture when not dark() "Oak and holly come down to the last field of {town}, and the field wall stops at them. A track goes in under the trees, wide enough once for a cart and now for one walker.".
  Observe {t}_wood_edge_dark at {t}_wood_edge as fixture when dark() "The trees are a black wall above the field. Nothing of the track under them can be seen without a light.".
  Observe {t}_wood_ride_scene at {t}_wood_ride as fixture when not dark() "The old ride runs straight between the oaks, grassed over, with holly closing in on both sides. Old stumps along it were cut long ago, and the wood has grown back over them.".
  // The stones are in sight from the ride by day: grey shapes up the slope under the beeches, a deer-path going up.
  Observe {t}_wood_ride_stones at {t}_wood_ride as fixture when not dark() "Up the slope ahead the oaks give way to beeches, and among them grey stones lie in a broken row along a mound. The slope goes up to them." teaches {t}_wood_stones_known.
  Observe {t}_wood_ride_dark at {t}_wood_ride as fixture when dark() "Under the trees the dark is complete. A heavy beast moves off through the holly, unhurried.".
  Observe {t}_wood_ride_mist at {t}_wood_ride as ambience when hour(clock) >= 5 and hour(clock) < 7 "Mist lies in the ride at the height of your knees. Three deer stand in it and watch you. Then they are gone.".
  Observe {t}_wood_ride_tracks at {t}_wood_ride as sign noticed by woodcraft when not knows(party, {t}_wood_tracks) "Where the ride is wet, cloven feet bigger than a pig's have churned the ground. A run goes off through the holly at the height of your hip. Its edges are rubbed with mud and bristle." teaches {t}_wood_tracks.
  Entity {t}_wood_tracks: fact "A boar's runs go off the old ride through the holly, to wherever it wallows.".
  Observe {t}_wood_burners_scene at {t}_wood_burners as fixture when true "A round clearing, black underfoot, with the rings of old charcoal-hearths in it and a hut of turf at the edge. Nobody has burned here for years. The hut's door hangs by one hinge.".
  Observe {t}_wood_wallow_scene at {t}_wood_wallow as fixture when true "A sunk place among alders, all mud, the trees round it rubbed bare and caked to the height of your chest. It smells of rank animal.".
  Observe {t}_wood_stones_scene at {t}_wood_stones as fixture when true "Under the beeches the ground rises to a long mound. Great stones lie fallen along it, grey and green with moss. They were set up in a row once, by {old}. Between two of them the earth has fallen in onto steps of dressed stone, going down into the dark. Cold air comes up them." teaches {t}_wood_door.
  Observe {t}_wood_stones_marks at {t}_wood_stones as sign noticed by lore when not knows(party, {t}_wood_mark) "On the inner face of one fallen stone is a mark cut in the way of {old}: a door, drawn shut. It is cut beside the steps, as a word is written over a door." teaches {t}_wood_mark.
  Entity {t}_wood_mark: fact "On a fallen stone beside the steps, {old} cut a door drawn shut.".
  Discovery {t}_wood_door "Between two of the fallen stones a slot goes down into the dark, with steps in it.".
  // The burners' hut: what they left, and why they left (found by searching here, or told by the herb-wife once she
  // trusts the company): a lamp, and on the bench the mark the old ones cut on the stones, which the shrine-keeper asks.
  Item {t}_wood_lamp "a burner's old lamp" is lantern at {t}_wood_burners hidden until {t}_wood_hut.
  // The oil the finding says is in it is there to burn (OR-685).
  Item {t}_wood_oil "the burner's lamp-oil, in a stoppered flask" is lamp_oil at {t}_wood_burners hidden until {t}_wood_hut.
  Discovery {t}_wood_stones_known "The old stones lie under the beeches above the old ride, up the slope from it, and a deer-path goes up to them from the burners' clearing.".
  Discovery {t}_wood_hut "Under the turf bench in the burners' hut is a lamp, and above it a mark scratched in the bench: a row of standing stones, and a door drawn shut." {
    Found by searching {t}_wood_burners "Under the turf bench in the hut is a lamp with oil still in it. Scratched into the bench above it are a row of standing stones and a mark like a shut door.".
  }
  Item {t}_wood_herbs "a stand of woundwort" is herbs at {t}_wood_ride hidden until {t}_wood_wort.
  Discovery {t}_wood_wort "Woundwort grows along the ride where the sun gets in." {
    Found by searching {t}_wood_ride "In a gap where an oak came down, the light gets in, and woundwort stands thick in it. You pick what you can carry.".
  }
  // The beast of the woods: it fights for its wallow, and it is there again a season later.
  Person {t}_wood_boar "the old boar of the woods" at {t}_wood_wallow {
    Role "a boar the size of a pony, grey on the back, one tusk broken off short". Species boar. Numbers 1. Level 2. Temperament territorial. Lair {t}_wood_wallow.
    Warns "The boar comes up out of the mud all at once. It stands and blows. It does not mean to go anywhere.".
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_wood_boar) to 100.
  // Asked, the one who buys what the woods give asks back, and tells what they know of the woods.
  Topic {t}_wood_asked with {dealer} "Ask {{dealer}} about the old woods" when true once {
    Says "'Have you been into the old woods?' says {{dealer}}, and looks at your boots. 'Go up by the field path, and keep to the old ride. Bring back woundwort, there's a price for it here. Keep away from the holly where the ground is churned, there's a boar that has had two dogs this year. And up the ride, where the beeches start, are the old stones. Nobody goes there. The burners went, and didn't burn in the woods again.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_wood_stones_known). }
  }
  // The one who buys what the woods give asks the company in turn (OR-850; src/campaign/put-questions.ts): what brings it
  // up to the woods, as soon as it is spoken with, and what it carries, once it has something green in its pack; and
  // teaches, for coin, how to read the woods, so that the old ride's tracks are seen there (woodcraft).
  Relation {t}_wood_met(group). Relation {t}_wood_shown(group).
  Topic {t}_wood_why with {dealer} "{{dealer}} asks what brings you to the woods" when addressed({dealer}, actor) once {
    Says "{{dealer}} looks at your boots before your face. 'You're not from here. What brings you up to the old woods?'".
    On discuss { Assert {t}_wood_met(actor). }
  }
  Topic {t}_wood_why_herbs with {dealer} "Say you have come for what grows there" answering {t}_wood_why when true {
    Says "'Woundwort, then,' says {{dealer}}. 'It grows on the old ride, in the gap where an oak came down and the sun gets in. Bring it here. There's a price for it.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_wood_wort). }
  }
  Topic {t}_wood_why_stones with {dealer} "Say you are going up to the old stones" answering {t}_wood_why when true {
    Says "{{dealer}} is quiet for a moment. 'Then keep to the ride. Where the beeches start, the slope goes up to them. And go to the shrine first. {{t}_priest} knows what is under the stones, and doesn't tell just anyone.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_wood_stones_known). }
  }
  Action {t}_wood_why_lie(actor: group, site: place) "Say you are only passing through" {
    Speaker {dealer}.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at({dealer}, site) and asks({dealer}, actor) and {t}_wood_met(actor).
    Time 1 minute.
    Resolve check(actor, deception, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, {t}_wood_tracks). }
    On failure { Assert knows(actor, {t}_wood_stones_known). }
    Result "'Then keep to the ride and out of the holly,' says {{dealer}}. 'A boar runs through it. It has had two dogs this year. Where the ground is churned, that's its run.'".
    Otherwise "'Passing through,' says {{dealer}}, and laughs. 'You've the stones in your face. Keep to the ride, then. The slope goes up to them where the beeches start. And see the shrine first.'".
  }
  Topic {t}_wood_plant with {dealer} "{{dealer}} asks about the herbs you carry" when addressed({dealer}, actor) and holding(actor, herbs) and {t}_wood_met(actor) once {
    Says "{{dealer}} has seen the green in your pack. 'Show me that. Do you know what you've got there?'".
    On discuss { Assert {t}_wood_shown(actor). }
  }
  Action {t}_wood_plant_named(actor: group, site: place) "Name the plant" {
    Speaker {dealer}.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at({dealer}, site) and asks({dealer}, actor) and {t}_wood_shown(actor).
    Time 1 minute.
    Resolve check(actor, woodcraft, dc_fair).
    On success { Give yarrow_poultice to actor. }
    Result "You turn a leaf over. Woundwort: the grey down under the leaf gives it away. {{dealer}} nods. 'Not many know it. Here. Yarrow, for the next one of you that bleeds.'".
    Otherwise "You call it sorrel. {{dealer}} turns a leaf over. 'Woundwort. See the grey under it? You'd walk past a field of it. I could teach you to read the woods, if you want it. Five coin.'".
  }
  Topic {t}_wood_plant_unknown with {dealer} "Say you do not know" answering {t}_wood_plant when true {
    Says "'Woundwort,' says {{dealer}}. 'For a wound that won't close. I could teach you to read the woods, if you want it. Five coin.'".
  }
  Action {t}_wood_lesson(actor: group, pupil: member, site: place) "Pay {{dealer}} 5 coin to teach {pupil} to read the woods" {
    Speaker {dealer}.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at({dealer}, site) and {t}_wood_met(actor) and memberOf(pupil, actor) and awake(pupil) and not brings(pupil, woodcraft) and quantity(actor, gold) >= 5.
    Time 6.
    Resolve tutor(pupil, woodcraft).
    On success { Decrease quantity(actor, gold) by 5. Increase quantity({dealer}, gold) by 5. }
    Result "{{dealer}} takes {pupil} out past the field wall for an hour. A deer's slot beside a boar's. The place a fox lay up. A broken stem a day old. 'Now you'll see what's in my woods,' {{dealer}} says.".
  }
  // The woundwort brought down is a fetch only until it is shown (OR-1503: an exchange, its crux understanding): shown
  // it, the herb-wife trusts the company with why the burners left the woods, which opens the hut in their clearing
  // (the lamp under the bench, gear by the way in) and tells what the old ones cut on the stones, which is what the
  // shrine-keeper asks before she says what lies under them (and so the place's name, which the old sayings of it and
  // her own grief at the king's door are asked by).
  Topic {t}_wood_burners_told with {dealer} "Ask {{dealer}} why the burners left the woods" when {t}_wood_shown(actor) and not knows(actor, {t}_wood_hut) once {
    Says "{{dealer}} puts the woundwort down. 'My father was the last of the burners. One night he took his lamp up to the old stones, to see what the old ones had cut there. He came down with the lamp out, and never lit it again, nor a hearth. A door is cut on the stone, he said, drawn shut, and shut for a reason. The lamp's under his bench in the hut still. Take it, if you're going up.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_wood_hut). Assert knows(actor, {t}_wood_mark). }
  }
  // The shrine-keeper tests what the company says it knows of the stones before telling what is under them (OR-851):
  // what the old ones cut there, a shut door (on the burners' bench, and on the stone itself), said or called to mind.
  // A wrong answer sends the company up to look; come back from the stones, it can say what it saw; and one who knows
  // the mark (seen on the stone by lore, or told by the herb-wife) can say it unasked.
  Relation {t}_rite_put(group). Relation {t}_rite_doubted(group).
  // A wrong answer is told something too (what would open her), so that the right one is not the only one the atlas
  // marks as teaching: the page had drawn "Say a door, drawn shut" blue among the three.
  // What she asks, kept as heard: the question is something to know, so that asking it is marked as worth asking.
  Entity {t}_rite_asks: fact "{{t}_priest} will say what lies under the fallen stones to one who can say what the old ones cut on them.".
  Entity {t}_rite_look: fact "{{t}_priest} will say what is under the fallen stones to one who has been up and seen what is cut on them.".
  Topic {t}_rite with {t}_priest "Ask {{t}_priest} what lies under the fallen stones" when knows(actor, {t}_wood_stones_known) and not knows(actor, {w}_named) once {
    Says "'So you know where the stones are,' says {{t}_priest}. 'Plenty say so. Tell me what the old ones cut on them, and I'll tell you what is under them.'".
    On discuss { Assert {t}_rite_put(actor). Assert knows(actor, {t}_rite_asks). }
  }
  Topic {t}_rite_sun with {t}_priest "Say a sun, rising" answering {t}_rite when true {
    Says "'A sun?' says {{t}_priest}. 'Then you haven't been up there. Go and look, and come back when you have.'".
    On discuss { Assert {t}_rite_doubted(actor). Assert knows(actor, {t}_rite_look). }
  }
  Topic {t}_rite_door with {t}_priest "Say a door, drawn shut" answering {t}_rite when true {
    Says "{{t}_priest} lets out a breath. 'Then you've seen it. Between two of the stones a stair goes down, into {site}. The dead there are older than {town}. Take light, and more than you think you need.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_wood_door). Assert knows(actor, {w}_named). }
  }
  Topic {t}_rite_hand with {t}_priest "Say an open hand" answering {t}_rite when true {
    Says "'Then you haven't looked,' says {{t}_priest}. 'Go up and look. Come back when you have.'".
    On discuss { Assert {t}_rite_doubted(actor). Assert knows(actor, {t}_rite_look). }
  }
  Action {t}_rite_recall(actor: group, site: place) "Think back to what the old makers cut on their doors" {
    Speaker {t}_priest.
    Requires able(actor) and at(actor, site) and at({t}_priest, site) and asks({t}_priest, actor) and {t}_rite_put(actor).
    Time 1 minute.
    Resolve check(actor, lore, dc_fair).
    On success { Assert knows(actor, {t}_wood_door). Assert knows(actor, {w}_named). }
    On failure { Assert {t}_rite_doubted(actor). Assert knows(actor, {t}_rite_look). }
    Result "The old makers marked a way down with a door drawn shut, to keep the living out. You say so. {{t}_priest} looks at you again. 'Then you know. Between two of the stones a stair goes down, into {site}. Take light, and more than you think you need.'".
    Otherwise "You try to call it to mind, and it won't come. 'Then go up and look,' says {{t}_priest}. 'Come back when you have.'".
  }
  Topic {t}_rite_again with {t}_priest "Tell {{t}_priest} a shut door is cut on the stones" when (({t}_rite_doubted(actor) and been(actor, {t}_wood_stones)) or knows(actor, {t}_wood_mark)) and not knows(actor, {w}_named) once {
    Says "'So it is,' says {{t}_priest}. 'Between two of the stones a stair goes down, into {site}. The dead there are older than {town}. Take light, and more than you think you need.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, {t}_wood_door). Assert knows(actor, {w}_named). }
  }
  // Where what is heard of the stones leads (OR-1040, OR-1501): up the ride to the stones, where the way down is seen;
  // and once it is known, down it. The shrine-keeper's question (what is cut on them) is answered on the way or not at
  // all: it tells what is under them (the place's name, which the herb-wife's old sayings and the shrine-keeper's own
  // grief about the king's door are asked by), not the way down, which no one needs telling once they stand there.
  Objective {t}_wood_go when knows(party, {t}_wood_stones_known) and not been(party, {t}_wood_stones) and not knows(party, {t}_wood_door) toward {t}_wood_stones "The old stones lie up the old ride, under the beeches. Nobody in {town} goes there.".
  Objective {t}_wood_answer when {t}_rite_put(party) and not {t}_rite_doubted(party) and not knows(party, {t}_wood_door) and not knows(party, {w}_named) toward {t}_priest "{{t}_priest} asks what the old ones cut on the fallen stones.".
  Objective {t}_wood_below when knows(party, {t}_wood_door) and not been(party, {w}) toward {w} "Between two of the fallen stones in the old woods a stair goes down into the dark. Take light, and more than you think you need.".
  // The woods go on without the company (OR-641), by the world's own clock: woundwort grows back on the ride a few
  // days after it is picked, twice, and not in winter; some nights after the old boar is killed a young one takes its
  // wallow; rain shows the boar's runs to anyone; and once the company has been down under the stones, the next wind
  // brings an oak down across the ride, with something in its roots.
  Measure {t}_wood_regrow(place). Relation {t}_wood_picked(place). Measure {t}_wood_boarless(place).
  Initially Set {t}_wood_boarless({t}_wood) to 5.
  Item {t}_wood_herbs2 "woundwort grown back" is herbs at elsewhere.
  Item {t}_wood_herbs3 "woundwort grown back" is herbs at elsewhere.
  Rule {t}_wood_bare when not at({t}_wood_herbs, {t}_wood_ride) and not at({t}_wood_herbs2, {t}_wood_ride) and not at({t}_wood_herbs3, {t}_wood_ride) and knows(party, {t}_wood_wort) and not {t}_wood_picked({t}_wood) and (at({t}_wood_herbs2, elsewhere) or at({t}_wood_herbs3, elsewhere)) { Assert {t}_wood_picked({t}_wood). Set {t}_wood_regrow({t}_wood) to 3. }
  Rule {t}_wood_growing when {t}_wood_picked({t}_wood) and untilLight(clock) == 1 and {t}_wood_regrow({t}_wood) > 0 { Decrease {t}_wood_regrow({t}_wood) by 1. }
  Rule {t}_wood_grown when {t}_wood_picked({t}_wood) and {t}_wood_regrow({t}_wood) == 0 and season(clock) != 4 and at({t}_wood_herbs2, elsewhere) { Retract {t}_wood_picked({t}_wood). Retract at({t}_wood_herbs2, elsewhere). Assert at({t}_wood_herbs2, {t}_wood_ride). }
  Rule {t}_wood_grown3 when {t}_wood_picked({t}_wood) and {t}_wood_regrow({t}_wood) == 0 and season(clock) != 4 and not at({t}_wood_herbs2, elsewhere) and at({t}_wood_herbs3, elsewhere) { Retract {t}_wood_picked({t}_wood). Retract at({t}_wood_herbs3, elsewhere). Assert at({t}_wood_herbs3, {t}_wood_ride). }
  Observe {t}_wood_regrown at {t}_wood_ride as sign when at({t}_wood_herbs2, {t}_wood_ride) or at({t}_wood_herbs3, {t}_wood_ride) "Where you picked the woundwort, it has come up again in the gap where the oak came down.".
  Person {t}_wood_young "a young boar" at elsewhere {
    Role "a young boar, black-bristled, that has taken the old one's wallow". Species boar. Numbers 1. Level 1. Temperament territorial. Lair {t}_wood_wallow.
  }
  Initially Set encounterXp({t}_wood_young) to 50.
  Rule {t}_wood_boar_days when not able({t}_wood_boar) and untilLight(clock) == 1 and {t}_wood_boarless({t}_wood) > 0 { Decrease {t}_wood_boarless({t}_wood) by 1. }
  Rule {t}_wood_boar_back when not able({t}_wood_boar) and {t}_wood_boarless({t}_wood) == 0 and at({t}_wood_young, elsewhere) and not at(party, {t}_wood_wallow) { Retract at({t}_wood_young, elsewhere). Assert at({t}_wood_young, {t}_wood_wallow). }
  Observe {t}_wood_young_sign at {t}_wood_ride as sign when at({t}_wood_young, {t}_wood_wallow) and able({t}_wood_young) "The runs through the holly are churned fresh. A new boar has taken the old one's wallow.".
  Topic {t}_wood_young_news with {dealer} "Ask {{dealer}} what is in the old woods now" when at({t}_wood_young, {t}_wood_wallow) and able({t}_wood_young) once {
    Says "'There's a young boar in the old one's wallow,' says {{dealer}}. 'Black as a coal, and no more sense than the last. Woundwort's come back on the ride, too, if you're going up.'".
  }
  Observe {t}_wood_ride_rain at {t}_wood_ride as sign when {!wet} and not knows(party, {t}_wood_tracks) "The rain has turned the ride to mud. The boar's runs show plain in it, going off through the holly." teaches {t}_wood_tracks.
  Item {t}_wood_windfall_ring "a ring of green bronze from the oak's roots" is grave_rings at elsewhere.
  Rule {t}_wood_windfall when been(party, {w}) and {!windy} and at({t}_wood_windfall_ring, elsewhere) and not at(party, {t}_wood_ride) { Retract at({t}_wood_windfall_ring, elsewhere). Assert at({t}_wood_windfall_ring, {t}_wood_ride). }
  Observe {t}_wood_windfall_seen at {t}_wood_ride as fixture when at({t}_wood_windfall_ring, {t}_wood_ride) "An oak has come down across the ride in the wind. Its roots stand up taller than you, and the torn earth under them is full of old stones.".
